# Voice assistant

This repo is **Pilar** (필라르), the user's personal Korean voice assistant. The name is Spanish for pillar. Call it `필라르` only — never `Hey Pilar` or `헤이 비서`.

It is **not** the hospital staff portal (`tjkimeye-staff`).

- Keep all files, caches, models, and venv under `D:\Projects\voice-assistant` (C: is full).
- The user wants minimum clicks. Do the work; report results.
- Do not deploy this project to Vercel.
- Do not edit `tjkimeye-staff` from this project.
- Voice flow: mic → wav → whisper.cpp → Korean text → `src/brain.py` → edge-tts.
- Always-on mode is `python -m src.main --watch`. It only answers when the utterance contains 필라르 / Pilar.
- Dangerous intents (delete, deploy, shutdown) must ask for `해도 돼` before doing anything. Do not actually delete files yet.
- Coding utterances go through `src/cursor_bridge.py` → Cursor SDK `Agent.prompt` (local, model composer-2.5) when `CURSOR_API_KEY` is set in `.env`. Otherwise queue to `runtime/cursor-queue.txt`.
- Default coding workspace is `D:\Projects\tjkimeye-staff` (`PILAR_WORKSPACE`). Never put the API key in git.
- Prefer verifying with `scripts/verify.py` (TTS→STT roundtrip) instead of asking the user to speak.
